==English==

===Noun===
{{en-noun|cups of tea}}

# A [[cup]] full of [[tea]].
#: ''Would you be a dear and get me a '''cup of tea''', please?''
# {{lb|en|idiomatic|singular only}} Whatever [[suit]]s or [[interest]]s one.
#: ''Daytime television is not my '''cup of tea'''.''

====Usage notes====
* The second sense is most commonly used in phrases such as, '''not my cup of tea''', '''just my cup of tea''', etc.

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|suitable interest}} {{l|en|bag}}, {{l|en|cup of coffee}}, {{l|en|cup of joe}}, see also [[Wikisaurus:predilection]]

